.TH PNG2VIRCON 1 "October 11, 2026" "Vircon32 DevTools 26.04.24" "Vircon32 Development Tools"
.SH NAME
png2vircon \- convert a PNG image into a Vircon32 texture
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B png2vircon
.RB [ \-o
.IR output.vtex ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.I input.png
.br
.B png2vircon
.B \-\-help
.br
.B png2vircon
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B png2vircon
converts a PNG image into a VTEX texture, the format
.BR packrom (1)
puts into a cartridge. Every kind of PNG is accepted: palette,
grayscale, RGB, with or without alpha, at 1 to 16 bits per channel. The
pixels are converted to 8-bit RGBA; an image without an alpha channel
becomes fully opaque, and a palette's transparent color becomes
transparent.
.PP
The Vircon32 GPU holds textures of up to 1024 by 1024 pixels.
.B png2vircon
itself does not check the size, but
.B packrom
rejects a larger texture. A texture is drawn through regions (see
.BR video.h (3v32));
to put many small images into one texture, use
.BR joinpngs (1)
first.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " output.vtex"
Write the texture to
.IR output.vtex .
Without
.BR \-o ,
the output path is the input path with its extension replaced by
.IR .vtex .
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose: report each step.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and author, and exit.
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
A VTEX file is a 16-byte header \(em the 8 characters
.BR V32\-VTEX ,
then the width and height in pixels as little-endian 32-bit integers
\(em followed by the pixels, row by row from the top, 4 bytes each in
the order red, green, blue, alpha.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The texture was written.
.TP
.B 1
Any error, printed as
.IR "png2vircon: error: description" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vircon2png (1),
.BR joinpngs (1),
.BR packrom (1),
.BR video.h (3v32)
.SH AUTHOR
The Vircon32 PNG importer was written by Javier Carracedo
.RI ( Carra ).
